I have to define the literal string type separately from its functionalities and I can't have a constructor out of the box eg:

```ts
type Currency = "USD" | "EUR";

function parse_currency(value: string): Currency {
  if (value === "USD" || value === "EUR") {
    return value;
  } else {
    throw new Error("Invalid currency");
  }
}

const currency = "USD" as Currency;
```

3. What workarounds are you using in the meantime?

none

